From: Midgy BALON <midgy971@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: sun4i-lradc-keys: set HOLD_KEY_EN for A523/r329

On the A523 (and r329) LRADC the CTRL register grew a dedicated
LRADC_HOLD_KEY_EN bit at bit 7, while bit 6 became LRADC_CHANNEL_EN.
The driver's HOLD_EN(x) macro writes bit 6, which on these SoCs only
toggles the (already-default-enabled) channel-enable, so hold-key
detection is never armed.

Without bit 7 set, a key press never raises the CHAN0_KEYDOWN pending
bit: the controller only reports DATA/KEYUP interrupts, so the IRQ fires
but no key-down event is ever emitted. The A523 User Manual programming
guide (sec 8.7.4) explicitly requires LRADC_HOLD_KEY_EN = 1 for normal,
single and continuous detecting modes alike.

Add a per-variant flag and OR in HOLD_KEY_EN(1) for the r329 variant.
Verified on a Trimui Smart Pro S (A523): with the bit set, Home / Volume
Up / Volume Down all report clean press (INTS=0x03, KEYDOWN) and release
(INTS=0x11, KEYUP); DATA0 codes 0x13/0x1e/0x29 map to 410/646/900 mV as
expected.

Assisted-by: Claude (Opus 4.8)
Signed-off-by: Midgy BALON <midgy971@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/input/keyboard/sun4i-lradc-keys.c b/drivers/input/keyboard/sun4i-lradc-keys.c
index 5730f08..792b23e 100644
--- a/drivers/input/keyboard/sun4i-lradc-keys.c
+++ b/drivers/input/keyboard/sun4i-lradc-keys.c
@@ -63,11 +63,13 @@
  * @divisor_numerator:		The numerator of lradc Vref internally divisor
  * @divisor_denominator:	The denominator of lradc Vref internally divisor
  * @has_clock_reset:		If the binding requires a clock and reset
+ * @set_hold_key_en:		Set HOLD_KEY_EN so a long-held key keeps reporting
  */
 struct lradc_variant {
 	u8 divisor_numerator;
 	u8 divisor_denominator;
 	bool has_clock_reset;
+	bool set_hold_key_en;
 };
 
 static const struct lradc_variant lradc_variant_a10 = {
@@ -84,6 +86,7 @@ static const struct lradc_variant lradc_variant_r329 = {
 	.divisor_numerator = 3,
 	.divisor_denominator = 4,
 	.has_clock_reset = true,
+	.set_hold_key_en = true,
 };
 
 struct sun4i_lradc_keymap {
@@ -149,6 +152,7 @@ static int sun4i_lradc_open(struct input_dev *dev)
 {
 	struct sun4i_lradc_data *lradc = input_get_drvdata(dev);
 	int error;
+	u32 ctrl;
 
 	error = regulator_enable(lradc->vref_supply);
 	if (error)
@@ -169,8 +173,14 @@ static int sun4i_lradc_open(struct input_dev *dev)
 	 * Set sample time to 4 ms / 250 Hz. Wait 2 * 4 ms for key to
 	 * stabilize on press, wait (1 + 1) * 4 ms for key release
 	 */
-	writel(FIRST_CONVERT_DLY(2) | LEVELA_B_CNT(1) | HOLD_EN(1) |
-		SAMPLE_RATE(0) | ENABLE(1), lradc->base + LRADC_CTRL);
+	ctrl = FIRST_CONVERT_DLY(2) | LEVELA_B_CNT(1) | HOLD_EN(1) |
+	       SAMPLE_RATE(0) | ENABLE(1);
+
+	/* r329/A523: keep reporting a held key (side buttons) via HOLD_KEY_EN */
+	if (lradc->variant->set_hold_key_en)
+		ctrl |= HOLD_KEY_EN(1);
+
+	writel(ctrl, lradc->base + LRADC_CTRL);
 
 	writel(CHAN0_KEYUP_IRQ | CHAN0_KEYDOWN_IRQ, lradc->base + LRADC_INTC);
 
--
2.43.0
